Public documentation pages only (no Google call with credentials), read by a research agent on 2026-10-21 and checked against the runtime design. Sources (docs.cloud.google.com; cloud.google.com 301-redirects there):
- live-api/start-manage-session: regional host, LlmBidiService path (v1), bearer token; session limits (audio 15 min without compression, connection ~10 min, goAway 60 s before end, resumption within 24 h); contextWindowCompression trigger_tokens 5k-128k.
- live-api/configure-language-voice: setup fields in snake_case in the samples (generation_config, speech_config.voice_config.prebuilt_voice_config.voice_name, input_audio_transcription, output_audio_transcription, realtime_input_config.automatic_activity_detection); 30 voices incl. Kore, Charon, Puck, Callirrhoe, Aoede, Zephyr, Leda.
- live-api/get-started-websocket: setup.model is the full model resource path; the sample's realtime input uses media_chunks with audio/pcm;rate=16000.
- live-api (overview) and models/gemini/3-8-live: audio in raw PCM16 16 kHz LE, out PCM16 24 kHz LE; gemini-3.8-live GA, released 2026-09-24, regions us, eu, us-central1; gemini-live-2.5-flash-native-audio GA, US and EU regions only, retires 2026-12-13; gemini-3.5-transcribe-live-preview is preview.
- learn/locations: lists Live models in every group, including Asia Pacific; this conflicts with the per-model pages, which are more specific.
- text-to-speech/docs/gemini-tts: Cloud TTS v1/text:synthesize with model_name, or Vertex generateContent with speech_config; regions global/us/eu/northamerica-northeast1; Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS preview only via the Gemini Enterprise API.
Not confirmed:
- whether Vertex accepts camelCase JSON on the websocket (proto JSON normally does; the runtime sends camelCase);
- the exact server message keys (setupComplete, serverContent.inputTranscription/outputTranscription, interrupted, usageMetadata);
- realtimeInput.audio versus mediaChunks (runtime default mediaChunks, switch with VERTEX_LIVE_AUDIO);
- whether interimInputTranscription exists on Vertex;
- a global host for Live.
